{"user": "b6 covers 2 lines. Good move?", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T21:33:44.293044+00:00", "assistant": "Not necessarily. In the endgame, \u201c2 lines\u201d can be a trap if it gives White a strong reply.\n\nFor **b6**, ask: after you place there, does White get a move like **a7** that flips a long diagonal/edge back? Also it doesn\u2019t take or secure a corner.\n\nSo I\u2019d be cautious with **b6**\u2014compare it to the other legal moves by asking which one leaves White with the fewest good replies, not which flips most now.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T21:33:53.538866+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T21:33:55.063477+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Prompt"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Negative Feedback": 1, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.6666666666666666, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Negative Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Prompt", "Neutral Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Prompt", "Negative Feedback"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "a